  "question": {
    "text": "The potential difference across a resistor is measured to be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;and the current through it is measured to be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>, then the value of the resistance <math><mi>R</mi></math> is"
